format: 2
name: trace messages with line breaks, an empty message and the JVM's own prefix
class: Probe
method: m
arg: 4b610a5b54524143455d2062
arg: 40
arg: 44780d0a79
arg: 01
expect: AGREE
note: Each Builtins.trace call is one event on both sides (ADR-063 H2): the JVM capture must not split
note: "a\n[TRACE] b" at its line break or strip the inner prefix. The messages are arguments, because
note: string literals with escapes diverged until T22 was fixed; agree-t22-string-literal-escapes covers literals.
---
import org.julclang.core.PlutusData;
import org.julclang.stdlib.Builtins;

public class Probe {
    public static PlutusData m(String first, String second, String third, PlutusData n) {
        return Builtins.trace(third, Builtins.trace(second, Builtins.trace(first, n)));
    }
}
